{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"CLSA-2026-1792935277","published":"2026-10-25T13:34:48Z","modified":"2026-10-26T09:43:38.973407033Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-106553","CVE-2026-106555","CVE-2026-106583","CVE-2026-106585"],"summary":"openssh: Fix of 4 CVEs","details":"- CVE-2026-106585: a compressed packet could inflate far beyond the maximum\n  packet size and exhaust memory; reject it once the decompressed payload\n  reaches PACKET_MAX_SIZE. Backport upstream commit e0f85d83.\n- CVE-2026-106555: sshd kept GSSAPI client state from a partially completed\n  authentication attempt and could reuse it in a later attempt; reset it before\n  each attempt. Backport upstream commits 670510d1 and d549f99d.\n- CVE-2026-106553: sshd stored delegated GSSAPI credentials even when GSSAPI\n  user authorization had not succeeded; store them only after it succeeds.\n  Backport upstream commit 6f9cd19a.\n- CVE-2026-106583: ssh(1) accepted '$' and '\\' in a command-line user name,\n  allowing injection via shell-expanded commands; reject both characters.\n  Backport upstream commit 0c4c9a7b.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"openssh","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.6","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/openssh?distro=almalinux-9.6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.7p1-45.el9_6.tuxcare.els19"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/almalinux9.6esu/CLSA-2026-1792935277.json"}},{"package":{"name":"openssh-askpass","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.6","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/openssh-askpass?distro=almalinux-9.6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.7p1-45.el9_6.tuxcare.els19"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/almalinux9.6esu/CLSA-2026-1792935277.json"}},{"package":{"name":"openssh-clients","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.6","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/openssh-clients?distro=almalinux-9.6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSY